---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How Courage for Kids handles your information.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated October 2026</em></p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you contact us, sign up to volunteer, or submit a partnership inquiry, we collect the details you choose to
        give us, such as your name, email address, phone number, and message. We use them only to respond to you and to
        coordinate your involvement with Courage for Kids.
      </p>

      <h2>Donations</h2>
      <p>
        Online donations are processed by third-party payment providers (such as Zeffy or PayPal) on their own secure
        pages. We receive your name, email, and gift details so we can thank you and send receipts. We never see or store
        your full card number.
      </p>

      <h2>What we never do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We never sell, rent, or trade your personal information.</li>
        <li>We never publish a child’s or family’s name, photo, or story without written permission from a parent or guardian.</li>
        <li>We don’t use advertising trackers on this website.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Many of our volunteers are students. If you are under 18, please have a parent or guardian review any form
        before you submit it. A parent or guardian can ask us to view or delete a minor’s information at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us to update or delete your information, or unsubscribe from our emails, by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page h1 { font-size: var(--step-4); }
  .prose-page h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-top: 2.25rem; }
  .prose-page li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>
